melody:
# Verse 1 (melody is pentatonic; "zing", "a", "was" and "but" take the B-G turn)
A-ma-zing grace, how sweet the sound,
D4 G4(2) B4/ ~G4/ B4(2) A4 G4(2) E4 D4(2)
that saved a wretch like me.
D4 G4(2) B4/ ~G4/ B4(2) A4 D5(3) ~D5(2)
I once was lost, but now am found,
B4 D5(2) B4/ ~G4/ B4(2) A4 G4(2) E4 D4(2)
was blind, but now I see.
D4 G4(2) B4/ ~G4/ B4(2) A4 G4(3) ~G4(2)

# Verse 2
'Twas grace that taught my heart to fear,
D4 G4(2) B4/ ~G4/ B4(2) A4 G4(2) E4 D4(2)
and grace my fears re-lieved;
D4 G4(2) B4/ ~G4/ B4(2) A4 D5(3) ~D5(2)
how pre-cious did that grace ap-pear
B4 D5(2) B4/ ~G4/ B4(2) A4 G4(2) E4 D4(2)
the hour I first be-lieved.
D4 G4(2) B4/ ~G4/ B4(2) A4 G4(3) ~G4(3)
